<title>USA: Mexico oil privatization faces opposition - official.</title>
<headline>Mexico oil privatization faces opposition - official.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican Secretary of Energy Jesus Reyes Heroles said on Wednesday there remains strong resistance within Mexico to opening the energy sector to the private sector, but that attitudes were changing.</p>
<p>Reyes Heroles, speaking at the Cambridge Energy Research Associates conference here, said a &quot;critical mass of public support&quot; was needed to make privatizations programs go forth.</p>
<p>&quot;There is still major resistance to...modifying the constitution in terms of the state being the sole producer of oil and all the hydrocarbons in Mexico,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
